    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Annie is disappointed that her family&apos;s vacation is postponed since her father has jury duty, and wonders why he simply doesn&apos;t skip it. Plato explains citizenship can reward good character, as shown in &quot;The Stone in the Road&quot; where those with and without it are repaid accordingly, and even if it doesn&apos;t, can make differences for the better, as the Roman Cincinnatus demonstrated by leading when and how he believed he must during war.</marc:subfield>
